{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["<b>You shall not take ransom, etc.</b> — The correct interpretation of this verse is as follows. At first, the verse warns us concerning the intentional murderer — 'You shall not take ransom,' meaning a monetary redemption for the life of a murderer who is liable to death, for under all circumstances he shall be put to death; he shall not escape death in any manner whatsoever, neither through exile nor through lashes or other punishments. Afterward it says, 'You shall not take ransom' from one who has fled and must return to the land until the death of the priest, returning to the subject of those obligated to exile, which it had previously mentioned, for they are the main subject of the passage. It is as though it says: And likewise you shall not take ransom from a murderer who has fled and must dwell in the land before the death of the priest. There was no need to say that we shall not take ransom so that he not flee there at all, for every killer of a life unwittingly will initially fear the blood avenger, lest he kill him in the heat of his heart or suspect him of being an intentional murderer, and he would not speak of ransom so that he not flee there at all. But after he has fled, he might speak of ransom to return to his land and not remain there all the days of the priest. And after he has fled and stood before the congregation for judgment and they have acquitted him, he will no longer fear, and then he may wish to return to his home before the appointed time — therefore the verse warns us against this. Alternatively, the letter vav may be absent from לָשׁוּב, and the meaning would be: or to return. But the first interpretation seems correct in my eyes."], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 35, :notes {0 "The phrase לָשׁוּב (\"to return\") in the verse וְלֹא תִקְחוּ כֹפֶר לָשׁוּב (Numbers 35:32) normally has no vav prefix; Ramban suggests reading it with a vav disjunctive (וְלָשׁוּב) — 'and to return' — or emending to אוֹ לָשׁוּב — 'or to return.'"}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:10:29.237026161Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}